# The trigger rate is the rate at which a held
# payment only covers the interest. For this
# plan it starts at 6.53%. After 6 months the
# trigger on the balance left is 6.607%. A path
# that stays just under that still runs: at
# 6.60% the payment of $2,147.67 still covers
# the interest, and the time to pay off stretches
# to the 100 year limit the language uses. A path
# that goes to 6.61% is refused: see
# examples/refused/trigger-crossed.renew.
# Renew does not model what a lender might do
# instead, such as raising the payment to at
# least the interest, converting the loan to a
# fixed rate, asking for a lump sum, or letting
# the balance grow up to a cap.

mortgage "Just under"
  balance $400,000
  rate 4.2% then 6.60% after 6 months payment held
  amortization 25 years
  term 3 years

show trigger rate of "Just under"
show payment of "Just under"
show payoff of "Just under"
explain "Just under"
